      "content": "That's a good summary of the sociological critique. However, some people argue that these tests are actually the only way to maintain a semblance of objectivity and that dismissing them entirely would just lead to even more nepotism and bias in hiring/admissions. Wouldn't it be more accurate to say that the problem isn't the tests themselves, but how we interpret them? Why is the critique so focused on the tools being \"invalid\" rather than just being \"imperfect\"?",
